  "reason": "The current best evidence is that multiprofile PCA RNA with ResNet50 image features, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion is the strongest setting (config_019, 0.639), but image-only performance is weak and only ResNet50 has been tested as the image encoder. config_025 changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the best profile, RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion, so it cleanly tests whether a stronger image representation can improve the promising multimodal pipeline. This is a high-value exploitation step: it may directly improve the best configuration and also clarifies whether further gains should come from image representation under the current best design."
